==In the TCG==
[[File:KindlerBrilliantStars170.jpg|200px|thumb|Full Art print of Kindler]]
{{main|Kindler (Brilliant Stars 143)}}
'''Kindler''' was introduced as a {{TCG|Supporter card}} in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] during the English Sword & Shield Series (the Japanese Sword & Shield Era). It was first released in the Japanese {{TCG|Star Birth}} expansion and the English {{TCG|Brilliant Stars}} expansion, with artwork by [[Hitoshi Ariga]]. It was also released as a {{TCG|Full Art card}} and {{TCG|Secret card}} in the same Japanese and English expansions, with artwork by the same artist. It allows the player to discard a {{TCG|Fire Energy}} card, then look at the top seven cards of their deck and put up to two of them into their hand.
{{-}}

==Trivia==
* In [[Pokémon GO]], "Kindler" is the name of an achievement {{GO|medal}} awarded for catching at least 10 {{type|Fire}} Pokémon.
* In [[Pokémon Champions]], the title of "Kindler" is awarded for winning ten battles using {{type|Fire}} Pokémon.

